  "content": {
    "story_lines": [
      "You are Wat, a turnip farmer.",
      "The old king has no heir, and",
      "the castle road is open today.",
      "",
      "A smith sells a rusty sword. A",
      "herald cries that the king",
      "seeks a champion.",
      "",
      "The knights laugh at your hoe,",
      "but their squire has the flu.",
      "Someone must carry the banner.",
      "",
      "The witch squints at your",
      "palm. ‘A crown or a noose,’",
      "she cackles. ‘Coin tips the",
      "scale.’",
      "A merchant’s cart is stuck in",
      "the mud. Bandits watch from",
      "the trees.",
      "",
      "The tourney is at noon. Entry",
      "needs a sword, or a noble who",
      "will vouch for you.",
      "",
      "A guard blocks the gate.",
      "Inside, the dying king is",
      "choosing an heir.",
      "",
      "Bandits ambush the knights.",
      "The banner falls in the mud",
      "and the captain is down.",
      "",
      "The knights win. The captain",
      "owes you his life and offers",
      "to take you to court.",
      "",
      "The outlaws cheer their new",
      "member. Tonight they rob the",
      "royal treasury.",
      "",
      "Gold glitters in the dark, and",
      "the royal seal lies on a",
      "velvet pillow.",
      "",
      "The cook shoves a tray at you.",
      "‘You’re late! The king wants",
      "his soup!’",
      "",
      "The soup is poisoned! The",
      "steward did it. Warn the king,",
      "or squeeze the steward?",
      "",
      "Noon. Your rusty sword against",
      "a duke in gold armor. The",
      "crowd is laughing.",
      "",
      "You win! The crowd roars, and",
      "the king calls his new",
      "champion to the throne room.",
      "",
      "The dying king studies you.",
      "‘Why should a farmer rule?’",
      "The whole court holds its",
      "breath.",
      "The king smiles and gives you",
      "his crown. The turnip farmer",
      "is king, and bread is cheap",
      "forever.",
      "With the seal you forge a",
      "decree. You rule, but every",
      "night you hear footsteps",
      "outside.",
      "The king names you his Hand.",
      "Not a crown, but the crown",
      "listens to you now.",
      "",
      "You trip on your own sword.",
      "The crowd loves it. You become",
      "the court jester.",
      "",
      "You go home to your turnips.",
      "They don’t ask why you came",
      "back.",
      "",
      "The sun sets. The king picks",
      "his cousin, and you are still",
      "a peasant with muddy boots.",
      "",
      "Guards drag you to the",
      "dungeon. Your cellmate also",
      "wanted to be king.",
      ""
    ],
